  "No conference calendar: the website has no calendar page (local events are pointed to a Facebook group), and its Wix event pages are mostly 2022-2025 (latest in window: Fall into Fitness, Oct 5, 2025). Events here come from the conference news blog (177 posts since Sep 2025, read one by one), the camp-meeting page, a registration page and Southwestern Union Record stories. Coverage is good for what was reported, but routine meetings (executive committee, board, pastors' meetings) are only visible when a post mentions them.",
  "What the news shows: a strong Hispanic track (Hispanic camp meeting 1,000+, Hispanic churches reported 240 baptisms in 2025, a Hispanic evangelistic caravan, new Spanish church plants in Bixby and Norman, Spanish evangelistic series), a Native Ministries health outreach (Diabetes Undone with the Choctaw, Okmulgee and Sallisaw churches, Tribal Health Conference booth, meal packing during the 2025 shutdown), Zomi and Myanmar congregations (Zomi camp meeting, youth fun day, VBS, children giving Bible studies door to door), and many summer VBS and community events in local churches.",
  "'Oklahoma Reconnect' (2026) is a conference-wide reclaiming movement: trainings (Midwest City; Tulsa Metro Oct 9-10, 2026 on reclaiming children) and 'Return Home' evangelistic series. The Reconnect article (posted Sep 14, 2026) dates the first training 'September 29', which cannot be right for a Sep 14 post; kept as printed and flagged.",
  "Regional town halls (Sep 25 - Oct 21, 2025) led to refreshed vision and mission statements (Feb 2026).",
